From 61f76ccc894f4e0535682d44be524aec76870f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 03:13:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 30/42] build: include multitenant module in Dockerfile.local +
 align Go directive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three small build-system gaps that the first kind E2E run
(TestMultiTenantSanity) surfaced. Each is independently low-risk;
together they are required for `make test-k8s-image` to actually
produce a binary against the multi-tenant patch tree.

1) transports/Dockerfile.local:
   The local Docker build copies every other workspace member into
   /build and `go work use`s them, but multitenant/ was added by
   patch 0001 without updating the Dockerfile. Result: the binary
   could never include the multitenant package — `make test-k8s-image`
   failed at `go build ./bifrost-http` with "no required module
   provides package github.com/maximhq/bifrost/multitenant".
   Fix: add `COPY multitenant/ ./multitenant/` and
   `go work use ./multitenant`.

2) multitenant/go.mod — `go 1.26.2`:
   The module declared `go 1.26.4` while every other workspace module
   uses 1.26.2. The Dockerfile pins golang:1.26.2-alpine3.23, which
   then refuses to build the module ("requires go >= 1.26.4"). Drop
   to 1.26.2 to match siblings; nothing in the module's source uses
   1.26.4-only features.

3) multitenant/go.mod — `replace framework => ../framework`:
   multitenant/go.mod had a `replace core => ../core` but no
   corresponding `replace` for framework. Inside the workspace this
   was fine because `go.work` covers both. In the Docker build,
   workspace mode still resolved framework via the local path — but
   the version-pin in `require framework v1.3.19` made Go reach out
   to the module proxy for that exact version's go.mod (to validate
   it), and v1.3.19 declares `go 1.26.4`. With the symmetric
   `replace`, Go uses the local copy's go.mod (which we just pinned
   to 1.26.2) for everything, no proxy round-trip.

After all three, `make test-k8s-image` produces a fresh
bifrost:local-test image from the patched tree end-to-end on a Go
1.26.2 base.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
---
 multitenant/go.mod          | 4 +++-
 transports/Dockerfile.local | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/multitenant/go.mod b/multitenant/go.mod
index 04e944ee4..aa090633a 100644
--- a/multitenant/go.mod
+++ b/multitenant/go.mod
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 module github.com/maximhq/bifrost/multitenant
 
-go 1.26.4
+go 1.26.2
 
 require (
 	github.com/maximhq/bifrost/core v1.5.19
@@ -159,3 +159,5 @@ require (
 )
 
 replace github.com/maximhq/bifrost/core => ../core
+
+replace github.com/maximhq/bifrost/framework => ../framework
diff --git a/transports/Dockerfile.local b/transports/Dockerfile.local
index 0fe524e84..b29591e90 100644
--- a/transports/Dockerfile.local
+++ b/transports/Dockerfile.local
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
   # Copy all local modules
   COPY core/ ./core/
   COPY framework/ ./framework/
+  COPY multitenant/ ./multitenant/
   COPY plugins/ ./plugins/
   COPY transports/ ./transports/
 
@@ -36,6 +37,7 @@
   RUN go work init && \
     go work use ./core && \
     go work use ./framework && \
+    go work use ./multitenant && \
     go work use ./plugins/compat && \
     go work use ./plugins/governance && \
     go work use ./plugins/jsonparser && \
